{"id":33802502335498,"type":"album","name":"Angel's Egg","artist":"Gong","year":1973,"weight":29,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710600.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-efd73820-a4c9-489a-b146-3264c60f630a/mbid-efd73820-a4c9-489a-b146-3264c60f630a-985466954.jpg","kind":"Album","tracks":13,"country":"GB","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"0XYFbtgXgis","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/0el78UTVnWvLJ9JTQxWQFy","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_kUWU00HKBaMqEccCwR-E7IPeKrF_h2M10","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/gong/angels-egg"},"desc":"This is the correct tag for Gong's fifth studio album, Angel's Egg. The album was originally released on Virgin Records in 1973. Angel's Egg is the second in Gong's Radio Gnome Invisible trilogy of albums, following Flying Teapot and preceding You. The trilogy forms a central part of the Gong mythology. The original vinyl album cover did not have an apostrophe in the title (although it was present on the center label of the LP). The original vinyl edition came with a booklet containing an extensive explanation of the mythology, including lyrics, a glossary of terms, and profiles of characters ."},"artist_ref":{"id":132076427907489,"name":"Gong","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Gong_2025.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":265524373450282,"type":"genre","name":"jazz","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":1461,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"},{"id":147423806094006,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":690,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":138197775829889,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":439,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":262736572970899,"type":"genre","name":"Space Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":282,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"},{"id":233393075954782,"type":"genre","name":"Canterbury Scene","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":213,"yt":null,"src":"musthear,rym"}],